# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 15-vm-boot: let this image also boot *inside* a VM.
#
# A bare-metal host does not need guest drivers, and the purist version of
# this config leaves them out.  That is the wrong trade: without them the
# fleet image cannot boot nested (an L1 host), cannot boot on a cloud instance
# during bring-up, and cannot be smoke-tested in CI without a second build.
# The cost is a few hundred KB of driver text that stays dormant on metal
# (virtio-pci simply finds no devices).
#
# Paravirt *optimizations* for running as a guest -- KVM_GUEST, PARAVIRT
# spinlocks, ptp_kvm -- are a different question and stay in opt-guest.config,
# because they change how the kernel behaves on bare metal too.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CONFIG_VIRTIO=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_MENU=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI_LEGACY=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_BLK=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_NET=y
CONFIG_VIRTIO_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_HW_RANDOM_VIRTIO=y
# Deliberately absent, even here: VIRTIO_INPUT and DRM_VIRTIO_GPU (no display
# on a host), 9P/NET_9P (use virtiofs), SCSI_VIRTIO (virtio-blk is the path).
